sched: hardware pressure on l4h

The l4h host publishes, per vCPU, the capacity other guests leave it on
its CPU and SMT siblings (l4h_event_page.host_cap); arch/l4h reports the
rest as arch_scale_hw_pressure().  The scheduler averages it only with
SCHED_HW_PRESSURE, which needs no cpufreq or thermal framework on l4h:
that code (pelt.c, avg_hw) depends on neither.

--- a/init/Kconfig
+++ b/init/Kconfig
@@ -609,8 +609,9 @@
 	bool
 	default y if ARM && ARM_CPU_TOPOLOGY
 	default y if ARM64
+	default y if L4H
 	depends on SMP
-	depends on CPU_FREQ_THERMAL
+	depends on CPU_FREQ_THERMAL || L4H
 	help
 	  Select this option to enable HW pressure accounting in the
 	  scheduler. HW pressure is the value conveyed to the scheduler
